# free — real-world examples

## Human-readable snapshot of RAM and swap

```sh
free -h
```

## Totals row for RAM + swap combined

```sh
free -ht
```

## Watch memory every 5 seconds while a Plex transcode runs

```sh
free -h -s 5
```

## Print 12 samples then exit (one minute of data)

```sh
free -h -s 5 -c 12
```

| Flag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| -b / -k / -m / -g | bytes / KiB / MiB / GiB |
| --tera | TiB |
| -h, --human | human-readable units |
| --si | powers of 1000 instead of 1024 |
| -l, --lohi | detailed low/high memory stats |
| -t, --total | totals row for RAM + swap |
| -s N | repeat every N seconds |
| -c N | repeat N times, then exit |

## Top memory consumers (free tells you how much; ps tells you who)

```sh
ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd,%mem,%cpu --sort=-%mem | head
ps -eo pmem,pcpu,vsize,pid,cmd | sort -k 1 -nr | head -5
```
